    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1007/s10640-026-01076-3",
      "sequence": 4,
      "source_sequence": 21,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Relocation of Toxic-Releasing Facilities and Effects on Environmental Inequality in the United States",
      "title_cn": "有毒排放设施迁移及其对美国环境不平等的影响",
      "authors": [
        "Xiao Wang",
        "George Deltas",
        "Madhu Khanna",
        "Xiang Bi"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "We investigate the impact of industrial facility relocation on the distribution of pollution incidence across different socioeconomic groups in the US. While facilities that relocated reduced their emissions by 68% relative to 1990, the extent of their reduction was 22% points lower than had they not relocated. We also find that most facilities moved to communities with lower income compared to their origin communities and that these facilities reduced their emissions by less than facilities that moved to higher income communities. Relocations resulted in larger emissions reductions in population dense locations, as facilities relocated primarily to lower density areas.",
      "abstract_cn": "我们研究了工业设施迁移对美国不同社会经济群体间污染分布的影响。虽然迁移的设施相对于68%年减少了1990的排放，但其减少幅度比未迁移情况下低22%个百分点。我们还发现，大多数设施迁往收入低于原社区的地区，且这些设施的减排量少于迁往高收入社区的设施。迁移导致人口密集地区的排放减少更多，因为设施主要迁往低密度地区。",
